    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d260-a7">

                <pb facs="0344" n="262" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg262"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 7.</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Fisher to Mr.
                        Portman</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Consulate of the United States of
                                America,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Kanagawa, Japan,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-09-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 11, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your communications Nos. 90 and 92, of the
                    7th and 9th instant, have been received, and will have my attention with the
                    governor of Kanagawa, &amp;c., as suggested, and I concur in opinion that this
                    is the better plan than to refer these claims to Yedo in the first instance.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEORGE S. FISHES, <hi rendition="#italic">United States
                        Cansul.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. L. C. Portman,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Charge d’Affaires ad interim, Yedo.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
